{"id": "unknown-2026-07-28-007", "date": "2026-07-28", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q3", "month": 7, "week": 31, "weekday": "Tue"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["supply_chain_shift"], "sentiment": {"label": "positive", "score": 0.5, "keywords": ["[否定]weak"]}, "importance": {"score": 0.5, "reasons": []}, "title": "Brent's 12% surge pushes Asian PFY Higher by up to 2.61%", "content": "PFY prices strengthened in Asia in the week ended July 24, with TexPro showing Chinese grades up 1.33-2.61 per cent and India's benchmark up 2.29 per cent.\nThe move was driven by a more than 12 per cent Brent crude rise, lifting naphtha, PTA, MEG and PET costs.\nPakistan's flat DTY and POY benchmarks signal weak mill demand, not stability, complicating sourcing decisions.", "sources": [{"name": "fibre2fashion_textile", "url": "https://www.fibre2fashion.com/news/textile-news/brent-s-12-surge-pushes-asian-pfy-higher-by-up-to-2-61--312120-newsdetails.htm", "type": "rss"}]}
{"id": "unknown-2026-07-28-008", "date": "2026-07-28", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q3", "month": 7, "week": 31, "weekday": "Tue"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["cotton_price"], "sentiment": {"label": "negative", "score": -0.5, "keywords": ["weak"]}, "importance": {"score": 0.5, "reasons": []}, "title": "ICE cotton closes higher on weaker dollar, technical buying", "content": "ICE cotton futures rose for a fifth straight session, with the December 2026 contract settling 0.90 cent higher at 80.88 cents per pound as a weaker US dollar, technical buying and strong Chinese reserve purchases supported prices.\nTight certified stocks also aided sentiment, while traders now await the US Federal Reserve, weather and export demand for further direction.", "sources": [{"name": "fibre2fashion_textile", "url": "https://www.fibre2fashion.com/news/textile-news/ice-cotton-closes-higher-on-weaker-dollar-technical-buying-312121-newsdetails.htm", "type": "rss"}]}
{"id": "unknown-2026-07-28-009", "date": "2026-07-28", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q3", "month": 7, "week": 31, "weekday": "Tue"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["cotton_price", "supply_chain_shift"], "sentiment": {"label": "neutral", "score": 0.0, "keywords": []}, "importance": {"score": 0.5, "reasons": []}, "title": "Asia's regenerated MMCF complex holds firm across the value chain", "content": "TexPro benchmarks for Asia’s specialty MMCF complex were unchanged in the week of July 20–24, with Modal fibre flat in China, India and Pakistan.\nModal, Liva Eco, Ecovero and Tencel yarn prices in 30/1 and 40/1 counts showed no week-on-week movement across the TexPro panel.\nStable contracts aid third-quarter sourcing plans, but tariffs, pulp and Pakistan energy costs remain watch points.", "sources": [{"name": "fibre2fashion_textile", "url": "https://www.fibre2fashion.com/news/textile-news/asia-s-regenerated-mmcf-complex-holds-firm-across-the-value-chain-312117-newsdetails.htm", "type": "rss"}]}
{"id": "lenzing-2026-07-28-010", "date": "2026-07-28", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q3", "month": 7, "week": 31, "weekday": "Tue"}, "entities": {"companies": ["lenzing"], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["earnings"], "sentiment": {"label": "neutral", "score": 0.0, "keywords": []}, "importance": {"score": 0.75, "reasons": ["涉及財報"]}, "title": "Austria’s Lenzing shifts focus to nonwovens, resets textiles strategy", "content": "Lenzing is accelerating its transformation by prioritising higher-margin nonwovens while reducing exposure to commodity textile fibres.\nThe strategy includes production consolidation, workforce reductions, €120 million (~$136.8 million) in savings and refinancing to strengthen profitability.\nThe company targets a 20–25 per cent EBITDA margin over the medium term.", "sources": [{"name": "fibre2fashion_textile", "url": "https://www.fibre2fashion.com/news/textile-news/austria-s-lenzing-shifts-focus-to-nonwovens-resets-textiles-strategy-312113-newsdetails.htm", "type": "rss"}]}
{"id": "unknown-2026-07-28-011", "date": "2026-07-28", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q3", "month": 7, "week": 31, "weekday": "Tue"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["earnings"], "sentiment": {"label": "negative", "score": -0.75, "keywords": ["decline", "weak"]}, "importance": {"score": 0.9, "reasons": ["涉及財報", "情緒極端"]}, "title": "Italian textile machinery orders rebound 25% in Q2 2026", "content": "Italian textile machinery orders signalled a gradual recovery in Q2 2026, rising 25 per cent from the previous quarter despite a slight year-on-year decline.\nStronger overseas demand continued to support the sector, while domestic investment remained weak.\nStable production backlogs and capacity use near 80 per cent suggested a steady outlook for the second half of 2026.", "sources": [{"name": "fibre2fashion_textile", "url": "https://www.fibre2fashion.com/news/textile-news/italian-textile-machinery-orders-rebound-25-in-q2-2026-312111-newsdetails.htm", "type": "rss"}]}
{"id": "unknown-2026-07-28-012", "date": "2026-07-28", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q3", "month": 7, "week": 31, "weekday": "Tue"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["supply_chain_shift"], "sentiment": {"label": "neutral", "score": 0.0, "keywords": []}, "importance": {"score": 0.5, "reasons": []}, "title": "Bangladesh targets production of 1.9 mn cotton bales by 2050", "content": "Bangladesh has set a 2050 roadmap to raise cotton lint output to 1.9 million bales, with an interim 500,000-bale target for 2030.\nThe plan targets lower import reliance for textile mills and export-oriented garment supply chains that need about 9 million bales a year.\nFarmer incentives, hybrid varieties, more acreage and credit support are central to delivery.", "sources": [{"name": "fibre2fashion_textile", "url": "https://www.fibre2fashion.com/news/textile-news/bangladesh-targets-production-of-1-9-mn-cotton-bales-by-2050-312099-newsdetails.htm", "type": "rss"}]}
{"id": "unknown-2026-07-28-013", "date": "2026-07-28", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q3", "month": 7, "week": 31, "weekday": "Tue"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["supply_chain_shift"], "sentiment": {"label": "positive", "score": 0.5, "keywords": ["growth"]}, "importance": {"score": 0.5, "reasons": []}, "title": "Bangladesh sets $63.4-bn FY27 export target aiming for 15% YoY growth", "content": "Bangladesh has set an export target of $63.4 billion for FY27, aiming for a 15-per cent growth over the income achieved in the last fiscal, Commerce Minister Khandaker Abdul Muktadir announced.\nOf the total, $55.2 billion is expected to come from merchandise exports, while the rest is projected to come from services exports.\nThe country failed to achieve its export target in the last fiscal. ", "sources": [{"name": "fibre2fashion_textile", "url": "https://www.fibre2fashion.com/news/textile-news/bangladesh-sets-63-4-bn-fy27-export-target-aiming-for-15-yoy-growth-312097-newsdetails.htm", "type": "rss"}]}
{"id": "unknown-2026-07-28-014", "date": "2026-07-28", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q3", "month": 7, "week": 31, "weekday": "Tue"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["supply_chain_shift"], "sentiment": {"label": "positive", "score": 0.5, "keywords": ["growth"]}, "importance": {"score": 0.5, "reasons": []}, "title": "Cambodia's growth eases as garment exports stay resilient in 2026", "content": "Cambodia's economy grew 5.3 per cent in 2025, with growth projected to moderate to 4.2 per cent in 2026 as energy costs and border disruptions weigh on activity, according to the AMRO.  \nGarment-led manufacturing exports and continued FDI remain key buffers for apparel supply chains.\nEnergy security, banking confidence, and higher value-added industry reforms are the next priorities.", "sources": [{"name": "fibre2fashion_apparel", "url": "https://www.fibre2fashion.com/news/apparel-news/cambodia-s-growth-eases-as-garment-exports-stay-resilient-in-2026-312118-newsdetails.htm", "type": "rss"}]}
